WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.440
A private German rocket just became the first to reach orbit from continental Europe, opening a new chapter for the continent's launch independence. This is Fascinating Frontiers, episode 185, the Spectrum Vehicle from Isar Aerospace climbed from the Andoya Space Center site in Norway. It settled into an elliptical path measuring 500 kilometers at its highest point and 180 kilometers at its lowest. No further announcements have described a burn

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:59.040
to circularize the path or any steps to release a payload. The European Space Agency has stated that this flight marks the first time an orbital vehicle has left the ground from the European mainland itself. Confirmation of the exact orbit still depends on public tracking records that the United States Space Force has not yet released. Next up, radio astronomers using a large Chinese dish have spotted two large pockets of hydrogen gas sitting near the whirlpool galaxy.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:17.920
The 500 meter aperture spherical telescope picked up the signals from each cloud. Every cloud holds an amount of neutral hydrogen equal to 3 million times the mass of the sun. Visible light images show nothing at those same positions and no newborn stars appear to be forming inside the gas.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:32.660
The measurements were described in a study released on August 4 in the journal Astronomy and Astrophysics. Those two clouds sit close enough to the whirlpool galaxy that their future evolution may be shaped by the larger spiral structure nearby.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:42.680
If every atom of neutral hydrogen inside one of those newly spotted clouds were gathered into a single ball, the sphere would still stretch across several light years.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:52.440
That same gas gives off a faint radio emission at 21 centimeters, a wavelength able to travel through thick layers of dust that block ordinary starlight.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:59.560
The wave can cross millions of years of space carrying details about how dense the material is and how it is moving.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:09.820
Telescope such as the 500 meter aperture spherical telescope received the signal long after it has crossed distances far larger than the width of our own Milky Way.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:18.740
Even with those maps in hand, the precise conditions that cause such a reservoir either to stay quiet or to begin forming stars remain unknown.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:32.860
Shifting to our own sky, the planet Venus is now sliding lower each evening as seen from Earth. It still appears briefly above the western horizon right after sunset, though it requires only a clear view toward the horizon.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:44.260
Later this year, the same planet will reappear in the morning sky before sunrise. No telescope or filter is needed to follow this change, only a spot with an open western sightline.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:55.360
Work has begun on a constellation of small satellites that China intends to place in low Earth orbit. The project centers on expanding the country's presence in that orbital regime.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:03.940
No launch dates have been announced for any of the planned spacecraft. Orbital parameters for the individual satellites have likewise not been released.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:12.880
The network is described as support for broader space infrastructure goals. 30 satellites form the target size of the overall constellation.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:21.020
Laboratory tests placed short protein chains into sulfuric acid mixtures that reproduce the chemistry of Venus cloud layers.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:31.040
The peptides remained intact after exposure to those acidic conditions. The outcome leaves room for complex chemistry to persist in the planet's upper cloud decks.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:43.100
Surface temperatures and pressures on Venus remain far too extreme for the same molecules to survive. Only the higher atmospheric layers reach temperatures and pressures that approach values familiar from Earth.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:56.360
The tests used mixtures calibrated to match the specific acid concentrations found in Venus clouds. Astronomers have started a search that targets moons around already known exoplanets instead of the planets themselves.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:07.700
The effort looks for satellites that follow stable orbits and maintain suitable surface conditions. Data from both ground-based telescopes and instruments in space feed into the analysis.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:18.180
No confirmed exo-moon candidates have emerged from the observations so far. The work examines whether such moons could sustain environments that allow liquid water to exist.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:30.940
Multiple telescope facilities contribute measurements of orbital stability and thermal balance. A visualization has been assembled to illustrate the path of asteroid apophis during its Earth approach in 2029.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:44.700
Position information supplied by the Jet Propulsion Laboratory Horizon Service underpins the sequence. The animation traces the asteroid's trajectory and marks locations where tidal forces could affect loose surface material.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.640
The sequence is intended as an illustration rather than a precise physical model of the asteroid's shape.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:05:02.120
Titles stretching and dust effects appear in the visualization as documented possibilities. The work draws directly on orbital data without attempting to render the body's exact topography.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:15.360
An amateur observer recorded a detailed image of the iris nebula with a compact smart telescope known as the C-star S-50. The final picture combined five hours and 40 seconds of total integration time.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:26.420
Twenty seconds sub-exposures taken in altitude asmeth mode built up the exposure stack. The image emphasizes the nebula's bright central region set against surrounding lanes of dust.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:37.260
The C-star S-50 captured the reflection nebula without additional equipment beyond the instrument itself. The result highlights fine structure in the dust that frames the luminous core.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:42.640
Over the past week, the program followed several longer running stories that continue to develop.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:53.620
ESA's juice spacecraft moved closer to its plan 2031 encounter with an untouched moon of Jupiter that may hold original material from the solar system's beginning.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:00.200
Blue Origin advanced construction of a large new facility meant to handle heavy payloads for upcoming flights.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:06.640
Sierra Space also confirmed the first cargo items booked for the opening flight of its Dream Chaser vehicle.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:12.680
Before we go, keep an eye on further updates from the ongoing search for moons around distant planets.

